# PCB Firmware Honesty Doctrine

**Tristan 2026-07-22/23 (mandatory):** Do not oversell virtual bring-up as “firmware tested and working on the design.”

## Canonical source

| Concern | Location |
|---|---|
| Status strings / forbidden claims | `src/lib/pdf-engine-v2/lib/pcb/pcb-firmware-honesty.ts` |
| Checked-in MCU bring-up | `firmware/pcb-bringup/` |
| Emit (copy tree + board binds) | `pcb-firmware-tier1-project.ts` |
| Excel labels (Terminal lane) | `build-excel-export.py::_pcb_firmware_status_string` |
| Pack layout | top-level `firmware/` in deliverable (sibling of `pcb/`) |

## NEVER

- Claim **FUNCTIONALLY VERIFIED** without a real HIL transcript
- Emit large C blobs only inside TypeScript — edit `firmware/pcb-bringup/`
- Treat Tier-2 host bind (Mach-O / `board_sim_native`) as MCU execution
- Print `CHECK … PASS` under QEMU without calling `virt_i2c_read8`
- Bury the only firmware copy under `pcb/firmware-mcu` / `pcb/firmware-other` in the emailable pack

## ALWAYS

- Max banner: **FAB-READY — UNPROVEN IN HARDWARE**
- Tier ≥3 status: **VIRTUAL BRING-UP PASS (QEMU + modelled I²C) — UNPROVEN IN HARDWARE**
- Fail closed if `firmware/pcb-bringup/` is missing from the git tree
- Empty modelled I²C bus → FAIL (not PASS)
- Gerbers under `pcb-boards/*/pcb/gerbers` (not only `pcb-project/`)

## Tier truth (quick)

| Tier | Is | Is not |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | Host contract harness | Silicon |
| 1 | Pinmap link from `firmware/pcb-bringup` | Running on MCU |
| 2 | Host net/device bind | Cortex-M execution |
| 3 | QEMU + `virt_i2c_read8` on RAM models | SAMD21 SERCOM / HIL |

